  "negation": {
    "_about": "A payment or code keyword (stages S3 and S4, and the signals ask_otp, ask_credential, ask_install) does not count when the caller is warning against it: 'Payment karne ko bol sakte hain, aap aise mat kariyega' or 'OTP kisi ko mat bataiye'. This is a WINDOW, not a blanket rule. A prohibition word (mat, never, don't, do not, should not, no need) negates a keyword when it is up to `before` words before it, or up to `after` words after it AND is followed within two words by a request verb (the window crosses a full stop on purpose). A plain 'nahin / not' negates only when a request verb follows it within two words ('payment nahin karni chahiye'), or when it follows 'zaroorat / need' ('karne ki zaroorat nahin hai'). So 'payment reflect nahin hua' (a demand) still counts. Known limit: a threat worded with a request verb ('payment nahin karna toh arrest') is read as a warning.",
    "before": 3,
    "after": 10,
    "prohibitions": ["mat", "मत", "never", "don t", "do not", "should not", "shouldn t", "no need", "dont", "मत"],
